    "color": "#0f7a5a",
    "visibility": "public",
    "description_md": "Hydrographic products DERIVED from the CalCOFI CTD cast profiles rather than measured: spice (spiciness at 0 dbar, TEOS-10) and the sensor-pair averaged sigma-theta at every published CTD depth; and, per cast, the mixed-layer depth (the CalCOFI legacy definition, with two alternative criteria beside it), the depth and value of the chlorophyll-a maximum and the chlorophyll-a integrated over the top 200 m, by the definitions of the CalCOFI CTD team. Computed from the full-resolution 1 m bins of the CalCOFI CTD Cast Files after the provider's quality flags are applied.\n",
    "keywords": ["EARTH SCIENCE > OCEANS > SALINITY/DENSITY > DENSITY", "EARTH SCIENCE > OCEANS > OCEAN CIRCULATION > OCEAN MIXED LAYER", "EARTH SCIENCE > OCEANS > OCEAN CHEMISTRY > CHLOROPHYLL"],
